            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0585" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg471"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1403a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-14T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>91. For General Russell.</p>
                <p>Please inform President Borno that the President has nominated Mr. John S. Hord
                    as Financial Adviser to Haiti in place of Mr. <pb facs="0586" n="472"
                        xml:id="pg472"/> McIlhenny, and request that Hord’s appointment, as in
                    similar cases, be made effective from this date.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
